<title>USA: U.S. light vehicle sales, company market shares.</title>
<headline>U.S. light vehicle sales, company market shares.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following chart shows total U.S. car and light truck sales and market share percentages for major automakers for the month of December and the full 1996 calendar year.</p>
<p>Percentage changes are based on daily selling rates. There were 25 selling days in both December 1996 and 1995, but there were 308 selling days in the full 1996 year and 306 selling days in 1995.</p>
<p>		Dec. 96	    Market  1996 Year	    Market</p>
<p> Maker	 Volume   % Chng  Share   Volume     % Chng  Share</p>
<p>=============================================================</p>
<p> GM	    341,494   -14.2   30.3   4,743,557    -2.7   31.3</p>
<p> Ford	  299,209   +10.6   26.5   3,843,438    +0.5   25.4</p>
<p> Chrysler    179,804    +1.1   16.0   2,450,826   +12.5   16.2</p>
